<SiteLayout path="/what-is-an-msp" title="What Is a Managed Service Provider? | Tech Judge Inc." description="Understand managed IT services, how an MSP differs from break/fix support, and what to consider when choosing an IT partner for your business.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="An introduction to managed IT" title="An IT partner." accent="Not just an IT fix." intro="A managed service provider, or MSP, takes ongoing responsibility for agreed parts of your technology environment, from monitoring and maintenance to support and security." />
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap narrow prose"><h2>What does “managed” mean?</h2><p>In a managed relationship, your provider maintains the systems within an agreed scope. The work includes routine care as well as responding to problems. That scope can cover employee devices, servers, cloud platforms, user support and security controls.</p><p>The important part is clarity. The agreement should explain what is included, when support is available, how incidents are handled and what work is quoted separately.</p><h2>A different operating model</h2><div class="comparison"><div><h3>Break / fix</h3><p>Help is typically requested after a problem appears. Work is scoped around that incident and often billed by the hour or project.</p></div><div><h3>Managed IT</h3><p>Monitoring, maintenance and support are part of an ongoing arrangement. The provider looks after the agreed environment over time.</p></div></div><h2>What should you ask a potential MSP?</h2><ul><li>Which users, devices, locations and platforms are in scope?</li><li>What support hours and response expectations are included?</li><li>Who owns accounts, credentials and documentation?</li><li>How are security incidents, backups and recovery handled?</li><li>Which projects, hardware and licenses are separate costs?</li><li>How will the service change as the business grows?</li></ul><h2>Can an MSP work with internal IT?</h2><p>Some businesses outsource most of their IT; others need help alongside an internal team. The responsibilities should be agreed around the people and systems already in place. An initial assessment is the right place to discuss that division of work.</p><h2>How Tech Judge fits</h2><p>Tech Judge’s offering brings managed IT, cybersecurity and cloud services together with C7-licensed infrastructure. That means office networking, cabling and physical security can be considered alongside the systems employees use every day.</p><a class="text-link" href="/it-and-cyber-security">Explore our managed IT services ↗</a></div></section>
  <ContactBand heading="Find the right level of support." topic="Managed IT & Cybersecurity" />
</SiteLayout>
